---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PRELAUNCH } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy · Sawaza" description="The Sawaza privacy policy: what Sawaza keeps, who sees it, and your rights." bodyId="page-privacy">
<style is:global>
#page-privacy .prose{max-width:min(100%,64em);columns:1}
#page-privacy .prose ul,#page-privacy .prose p{max-width:56em}
#page-privacy .prose .sum{max-width:56em;margin:28px 0 8px;padding:22px 24px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line)}
#page-privacy .prose .sum h2{margin-top:0;font-size:clamp(20px,2.4vw,26px)}
#page-privacy .prose .next-row .tlink{min-height:44px}
#page-privacy .draft{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:18px 20px;border-radius:14px;border:1.5px dashed rgba(227,168,43,.6);background:var(--goldsoft);color:var(--ink);font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;margin-bottom:28px}
#page-privacy .draft .placeholder{flex:none;margin-top:3px}
#page-privacy .prose .pending{color:var(--quiet);font-size:15px}
#page-privacy .prose .pending .placeholder{margin-right:6px}
#page-privacy .prose h2:first-of-type{margin-top:28px}
</style>
<section class="page-hero" id="top">
  <svg class="watermark" viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="currentColor"><path d="M113.394,690.625 L237.500,690.625 A184.375,190.625 0 0 0 421.875,500.000 A340.625,334.375 0 0 1 762.500,165.625 L810.606,165.625 A25.000,25.000 0 0 0 826.950,121.712 A500.000,500.000 0 0 0 12.163,609.619 A103.750,103.750 0 0 0 113.394,690.625 Z"/><path d="M886.606,309.375 L762.500,309.375 A184.375,190.625 0 0 0 578.125,500.000 A340.625,334.375 0 0 1 237.500,834.375 L189.394,834.375 A25.000,25.000 0 0 0 173.050,878.288 A500.000,500.000 0 0 0 987.837,390.381 A103.750,103.750 0 0 0 886.606,309.375 Z"/></g></svg>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="q">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1>Your records, <em>your</em> choice.</h1>
      <p class="sub" data-new="1">What Sawaza keeps, who sees it, and what we never do with it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="prose">
  <p class="meta">Last updated 28 October 2026</p>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2><p data-new="1">Sawaza is made by SAWAZA TECHNOLOGIES - SMC LIMITED, a company registered in Uganda under registration number 80047057968423, with its registered office at Buloba, Wakiso District, P.O. Box 216499 Kampala. In this policy, "Sawaza", "we" and "us" mean that company, and "you" means the person using the Sawaza app or this website.</p><p data-new="1">We decide what personal data the app collects and why, so we are responsible for it under the Data Protection and Privacy Act, 2019 of Uganda. Questions about this policy go to hello@sawaza.app.</p><h2>2. What we collect</h2><p data-new="1">We collect only what the app needs to keep a record both sides can sign:</p><ul data-new="1"><li><b>Your phone number.</b> It is how you sign in and how other people find you on Sawaza. We confirm it with a one-time code.</li><li><b>The name and photo you give us.</b> Others see them on records you share with them and in groups you join.</li><li><b>Your records.</b> What you write: the amount, the item, the date, the other party, any note or picture you attach, and each side's answer and signature.</li><li><b>Your own lists.</b> The contacts, spaces, items, balances, groups and accounts you keep in the app.</li><li><b>Device details.</b> A token so we can send you notifications, a check that the app talking to us is the real one, and crash reports with the phone model and app version, so we can fix faults.</li></ul><p data-new="1">We do not collect your location, we do not track you across other apps or websites, and this website sets no advertising cookies.</p><h2>3. Your phonebook</h2><p data-new="1">If you allow it, the app reads your phonebook on your phone so it can show names you already know. Your phonebook is read and held on your phone only. We do not upload it, store it or share it.</p><p data-new="1">When you choose one person to send a record to or invite to a group, we receive that one number so the record or invitation can reach them. The name you saved them under stays yours: on a group's roster and on the other person's phone, your private label for them is never shown.</p><h2>4. Who sees your records</h2><p data-new="1">A record is private to you until you send it. You can keep records for yourself and never share them.</p><ul data-new="1"><li><b>When you send a record</b>, the person it names sees that record, and only that record.</li><li><b>If they are not on Sawaza yet</b>, they get a link to that one record. The link opens a short preview of that one record (the sender's name, what it was for, the amount and the date) for a limited time. It shows no phone numbers, notes or pictures, and it closes once the record is answered or after a day.</li><li><b>In a group</b>, every member reads the group's records, and its officers write them.</li><li><b>In a business account</b>, the people the business names read and write its records according to their role.</li><li><b>We do not show your records to anyone else</b>, and other users cannot search for them.</li></ul><p data-new="1">People you share a record with may keep their own copy, as they would a paper receipt.</p><h2>5. Why we use your data</h2><p data-new="1">We use your data to run Sawaza for you: to sign you in, to deliver records and invitations, to let both sides sign, to keep your copy safe, to send the notifications you allow, and to fix faults. We rely on the agreement between us under our terms to do this, and on your consent where we ask for it, such as for your phonebook and notifications. You can withdraw consent in your phone's settings at any time.</p><h2>6. What we never do</h2><p data-new="1">We do not sell your data, we do not rent it out, and we do not show you ads.</p><p data-new="1">Sawaza holds no funds and moves no money, so we never ask for your bank or mobile money details. Sawaza never asks you to send money.</p><h2>7. Who processes data for us</h2><p data-new="1">We use Google Firebase, a cloud service run by Google, to store records, sign people in, send notifications and receive crash reports. Google processes this data for us under its own data protection terms and may not use it for its own purposes. Our servers currently run in Google's data centres in Europe, which means your data leaves Uganda. We do this with the safeguards the law requires, and only with providers that protect data to at least the standard of Ugandan law.</p><p data-new="1">We may disclose data where the law requires it, for example to answer a valid court order. We will tell you when the law allows us to.</p><h2>8. How long we keep it</h2><p data-new="1">We keep your data while your account is open. When you delete your account from Settings, we erase your name, photo, contacts, items and every record not yet confirmed, and sign you out at once.</p><p data-new="1">Records that were confirmed with somebody else stay, because they belong to both sides: the other person keeps their copy, and your side shows as a deleted account with no name. Crash reports are deleted after 90 days.</p><h2>9. How we protect it</h2><p data-new="1">Data travels encrypted between your phone and our servers, and is encrypted where it is stored. Each record is signed on each side's own phone, so a change to a signed record would show. Access to our systems is limited to the people who need it to run Sawaza.</p><h2>10. Your rights</h2><p data-new="1">Under the Data Protection and Privacy Act, 2019, you may ask us:</p><ul data-new="1"><li>to tell you what data we hold about you and give you a copy;</li><li>to correct data that is wrong;</li><li>to delete your data, which you can also do yourself from Settings;</li><li>to stop using your data for a purpose you object to.</li></ul><p data-new="1">Write to hello@sawaza.app from the app or with your Sawaza phone number, and we will answer within 30 days. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Personal Data Protection Office of Uganda.</p><h2>11. Children</h2><p data-new="1">Sawaza is for people aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect data from children. If you believe a child has an account, tell us and we will delete it.</p><h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2><p data-new="1">If we change this policy, we will post the new version here with its date. If a change affects how your data is used, we will tell you in the app before it takes effect.</p>
  <div class="next-row"><a class="tlink" href="/terms">Terms <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>{PRELAUNCH ? <a class="tlink" href="/#contact">Contact <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a> : <a class="tlink" href="/trust">Trust and privacy <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>}</div>
</div></div></section>
</Base>
